cpp std.cin, c stdio.stdin and rust's whole std::io::Stdin surface were already
ipc_recv -- same family, same shape, three languages right and five wrong, which
is what makes this drift and not an unmade decision. It is INV-nular's rule in
the RECALL direction where the ADR-0049 campaign has been sweeping the precision
direction; counting them together would let the campaign report progress while
the recall hole grows.

THE SCOPE LINE IS THE ARGUMENT. A read that takes a STREAM -- fgets, fscanf,
getc, fread, System.IO.hGetLine, java.util.Scanner.nextLine,
bufio.Reader.ReadString -- crosses whatever that stream is attached to, which
INV-zumin classes as undecidable at the call site and INV-bagok holds open. None
moved. INV-zumin recorded that multiplying such rows is "actively wrong ... the
expensive direction", so the remedy there is inference (WI-lipis), not a
boundary swap. TestArgumentConditionedReadsDidNotMove fails if the line moves.

"Scan" joins go's ambiguous_names in the same change and that is not incidental:
fmt.Scan and bufio.Scanner.Scan share a short name, and Go leaves an untyped
receiver with NO module hint, so the row without the guard would have tagged
every sc.Scan() in every Go program as a stdin read -- manufacturing exactly the
false sources this commit is the mirror of. Pinned both ways.

