This is a TWO-language recall fix and a FIVE-language correctness fix; the two
numbers are stated separately. The new mainstream test pins only the two live
arms, because pinning the three dead ones would pin a bug in place.

CORPUS EFFECT IS ZERO AND IS REPORTED, NOT BURIED. Six repositories re-classified
under both catalogues in one process with the analyzer run once (shellcheck,
tmate, tmux, caddy, jaeger, hypergumbo): not one boundary tag changes. A uniform
zero across six repos is the signature of a broken probe, so the before-arm was
positive-controlled first -- it returns fs_read for scala.io.StdIn.readLine where
the after-arm returns ipc_recv. The population is genuinely that thin:
word-boundary greps find ONE real getLine in shellcheck and ZERO
getchar/scanf/gets in tmux, against 28 substring "hits" that are sscanf and
fgets. Both numbers are recorded so the loose one cannot be quoted alone.

ALSO FIXED, AND IT IS WHY THE ABOVE COULD BE TRUSTED: a catalogue-only change
selected TWO test files, both of them ones this commit adds. smart-test slices on
^packages/.*/src/.*\.py$ and a YAML catalogue is not a Python source file, so CI
-- which runs the committed manifest -- would not have run the io-boundary or
taint suites on a change that moves rows between boundaries in five languages.
That is INV-kafak's defect in a second change class, so it gets INV-kafak's fix:
a change under io_primitives/ or io_primitives_overlays/ unions every test naming
load_catalog, io_primitives or io_boundary, found by grep across package and root
test directories. 104 files select where 2 did. The three spellings are not
ASSUMED load-bearing -- a test measures that each arm selects something and that
the union properly exceeds at least one arm, because that exact claim about the
doc gate was refuted the first time it was checked.

One row was left wrong on purpose: haskell Prelude.readIO is fs_read and its type
is String -> IO a, so it parses a value already in hand and crosses nothing --
INV-zumin class (d), which that item says needs its own item rather than being
absorbed by a neighbouring fix. Filed as INV-savuk, with a note in the row saying
why. Its sibling readLn (= getLine >>= readIO) did move: the composite crosses
and the parser it delegates to does not.

